# .dockerignore — .gitignore does NOT control the Docker build context,
# so large or host-specific artifacts are excluded explicitly here.
#
# Rationale for the non-obvious entries:
#  * Dimuon_DoubleMu.csv IS tracked in git but must NOT be baked into the image:
#    the image is ~1.5 GB of wheels and a 14 MB dataset on top of it buys nothing,
#    and src/data_download.py fetches (and checksum-verifies) it at run time.
#  * models/ and *.joblib are regenerated by the default CMD, so shipping stale
#    weights from the host would silently mask a broken training step.
#  * results/ and logs/ are outputs of the run, not inputs to it.

# --- VCS / CI metadata ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python build & cache artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- Secrets / local config ---
.env
*.pem
*.key

# --- Datasets and model binaries (regenerated inside the container) ---
*.csv
*.root
*.root.fingerprint
*.joblib
*.pt
*.onnx
*.pkl
models/

# --- Run outputs (produced by the container CMD) ---
plots/
results/
logs/
temp/
run_output.txt
clean.txt

# --- Docs not needed at runtime ---
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
